{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_2df15321b834fb238903d703b71eed053b9c43e925d1378b30a0e0c7621ab075", "title": "Daryl Katz", "text": "Daryl Allan Katz (born May 31, 1961) is a Canadian businessman, investor, and philanthropist. With an estimated net worth of $US 4.14 billion (as of November 2015), Katz was ranked by \"Forbes\" as the 12th wealthiest Canadian and 534th in the world. The Edmonton-based Katz is founder and chairman of the Katz Group of Companies, one of Canada’s largest privately owned enterprises, with operations in the pharmacy, sports & entertainment, and real estate development sectors. Katz Group owns the Edmonton Oilers, and is leading the development of Rogers Place arena and the Ice District. Katz is a former lawyer, and resides in Edmonton.", "score": 32.7433}, {"id": "hp_doc_fc3be9534829d40f0bf6fca0020d6ecde807d0d8d9278115f9d1187b22b2ba3b", "title": "N. Murray Edwards", "text": "N. Murray Edwards {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (born December 10, 1959) is a Canadian oil sands financier and a co-owner of the Calgary Flames hockey team. With an estimated net worth of $US 2.2 billion (as of March 2011), Edwards was ranked by \"Forbes\" as the 14th wealthiest Canadian and 540th in the world. Edwards launched major Canadian companies including Canadian stalwarts Canadian Natural Resources Ltd and Ensign Energy Services Inc.", "score": 11.8808}, {"id": "hp_doc_16665f7bffe3065a5d027e4ce5e23b9ce01a8ec7533e9c8a327cb8908a424c9f", "title": "Daryl Sabara", "text": "Daryl Christopher Sabara (born June 14, 1992) is an American actor, perhaps best known for playing Juni Cortez in the \"Spy Kids\" film series, as well as for a variety of television and film appearances, including \"Generator Rex\", \"Wizards of Waverly Place\", \"Father of the Pride\", \"The Polar Express\", \"Keeping Up with the Steins\", \"Halloween\", and \"America's Most Talented Kids\" (on which he was a judge).", "score": 10.0726}], "remaining_searches": 1}
